# Oldroyd-B confined-sphere 3D smoke for the KRK-VE-3D dispatch wiring.
# The production driver (run_conformation_sphere_libb_3d) rebuilds the
# sphere geometry analytically from N, radius, and (optional) cx/cy/cz; the
# Domain/Obstacle/Boundary below name the case and supply those scalars.
#
# Tiny grid, R=4 (cut-links exercised), parabolic-y inlet. With u_in=0.04
# the centreline u_ref = (2/3)*u_in = 0.02667, so Wi = lambda*u_ref/R = 0.01
# at lambda = 1.5; beta = nu_s/(nu_s+nu_p) = 0.5.
Simulation sphere_oldroyd_b D3Q19

Define R = 4
Define u_in = 0.04
Define cx = 12
Define cy = 12
Define cz = 12

Domain L = 48 x 24 x 24  N = 48 x 24 x 24
Physics R = R u_in = u_in cx = cx cy = cy cz = cz
Rheology oldroyd_b { nu_s = 0.04 nu_p = 0.04 lambda = 1.5 }
Module viscoelastic

Obstacle sphere wall(radius = R) { (x - cx)^2 + (y - cy)^2 + (z - cz)^2 <= R^2 }
Boundary west  velocity(ux = u_in, uy = 0)
Boundary east  pressure(rho = 1)
Boundary south wall
Boundary north wall

Run 20 steps
